const FACTS = ["Carrots were mostly purple long ago! Orange carrots came later, and they're full of vitamin A, which helps your eyes see in the dark.", "A strawberry wears its seeds on the outside. There are about two hundred tiny seeds on every berry!", "Sea otters hold hands while they sleep, so they don't float away from each other.", "Broccoli is really a bunch of tiny flowers that haven't opened yet. When you eat broccoli, you're eating a bouquet!", "Honey never goes off. Pots of honey found in ancient Egyptian tombs were still good after three thousand years.", "Your brain uses about a fifth of all your body's energy. So breakfast really is brain fuel!", "Octopuses have three hearts, and their blood is blue.", "Every pea is a seed. Plant one, and it could grow into a whole new pea plant!", "A fluffy cloud can weigh as much as a hundred elephants. It floats because the water is spread out into tiny droplets.", "Spinach has iron, which helps your blood carry oxygen around your body. That's why the cartoon sailor ate it to get strong.", "Butterflies taste with their feet!", "A kiwi fruit has more vitamin C than an orange. Vitamin C helps your body heal cuts and fight off colds.", "Elephants can feel rumbles in the ground through their feet, so they can sense other elephants far away.", "When you laugh with friends, your body makes chemicals that help you feel happier and calmer.", "There are no wild snakes in Ireland at all.", "Apples float in water because about a quarter of an apple is air. That's why bobbing for apples works!", "A group of flamingos is called a flamboyance. Flamingos are pink because of the shrimp and algae they eat.", "Sweet potatoes, pumpkins and carrots are orange because of beta carotene, which your body turns into vitamin A for healthy skin and eyes.", "Hummingbirds are the only birds that can fly backwards.", "A dog's nose print is unique, just like your fingerprint.", "Scientists have found that noticing three good things each day can help people feel happier.", "Blueberries are one of the very few foods that are naturally blue.", "Avocados are a type of berry, but strawberries are not true berries at all!", "The Eiffel Tower grows about fifteen centimetres taller in summer, because metal stretches when it gets hot.", "Tomatoes were once thought to be poisonous in Europe. Now they're in pizza, soup and salads all over the world!", "Some penguins give each other pebbles as presents.", "A day on Venus is longer than a year on Venus. It spins so slowly that it goes all the way round the Sun before it finishes one turn!", "Raspberries, apples, pears and strawberries all belong to the rose family.", "Cucumbers are about ninety six percent water, so they're a great crunchy snack on a hot day.", "Wombats do poos shaped like little cubes!", "A red pepper has more than twice as much vitamin C as an orange.", "A group of owls is called a parliament.", "Koalas can sleep for up to twenty hours a day.", "A giraffe's long neck has just seven bones, the same number as yours!", "A pineapple takes about two years to grow.", "A blue whale's heart is about the size of a dodgem car.", "Smiles are catching! When you smile at someone, they often smile back without even thinking about it.", "A bolt of lightning is about five times hotter than the surface of the Sun.", "Mushrooms aren't plants. They're actually more closely related to animals!", "Beans and lentils are full of protein, which helps your muscles grow strong for running and jumping.", "Newgrange in County Meath is older than the pyramids of Egypt. On the shortest day of the year, sunlight shines right into its secret inner room.", "Honeybees do a waggle dance to tell the other bees where the best flowers are.", "Puffins nest around the coast of Ireland, and many of them come back to the very same burrow year after year.", "The fruit came first! The colour orange was named after the orange fruit.", "Your stomach gets a brand new lining every few days, so it never digests itself.", "A single teaspoon of garden soil can hold more tiny living things than there are people on Earth.", "Bananas give you lots of quick energy, which is why tennis players often eat them between games.", "A snail can have thousands of tiny teeth on its tongue.", "Sharks were around before the dinosaurs, and before trees!", "Kind words really matter. Helping someone else gives your own brain a little boost of happiness too."];
